		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3106&amp;p=24857#p24857"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I have a gd77 radio with v1.1.8 fw is it safe to load the open gd77 firmware to it? I am having no luck finding the update.exe file needed to update the fw to 4.3.6.</div></blockquote>Yous post doesn't make any sense.<br><br>The OpenGD77 project does not a file called update.exe<br><br><br>It doesn't matter what version of official firmware is already on the radio. The firmware gets completely overwritten when you use the OpenGD77 to install OpenGD77 onto the radio.<br><br>It is not necessary or advisable to change to another official version before installing the OpenGD77 firmware, becuase the official firmware versions occasionally have a nasty habit of bricking the radio when you change from one official version to another official version.<br><br>You do need the official firmware version 4.3.6 binary file, but only to act as a Donor for the DMR codec. This is for legal reasons associated with the codec.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Aug 07, 2023 3:02 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
